Daniel’s comment about one-sided contamination made me wonder what would happen if there were false positives that were not accounted for in the model.  The pattern that Marc showed in the original e-mail persists after changing the simOcc function to include some observation-level false positives (see fig). It makes sense that it does because false detections in sites that do not have the species must blur the relationship with the covariates. There are different sorts of two-sided contaminations.

